From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] eccci: include scheduler clock API explicitly

Linux 6.18 no longer provides local_clock() through the headers pulled in by
ccci_hif.c. Include its declaring header directly.

This is a compile-only compatibility change and does not enable the modem at
runtime.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/types.h>
+#include <linux/sched/clock.h>
 #include <linux/ktime.h>
 
 #include "ccci_debug.h"
-- 
2.50.1
